\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord! it is good for us to be
\par High on the mountain here with Thee:
\par Here in an ampler, purer air,
\par Above the stir of toil and care
\par Of hearts oppressed with doubt and grief,
\par Believing in their unbelief,
\par Calling Thy servants all in vain
\par To ease them of their bitter pain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lord!  it is good for us to be
\par With Thee, and with Thy faithful three:
\par Here, where the apostle's heart of rock
\par Is nerved against temptation's shock;
\par Here, where the son, of thunder learns
\par The thought that  breathes, the word that burns;
\par Here, where on eagle's wings we move
\par With him whose last, best word is love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord! it is good for us to be
\par Entranced, enwrapped, alone with Thee,
\par Watching the glistening raiment glow
\par Whither than Hermon's whitest snow,
\par The human lineaments which shine
\par Irradiant with a light divine,
\par Till we, too, change from grace to grace,
\par Gazing on that transfigured face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord! it is good for us to be
\par Here on the holy mount with Thee,
\par When darkling in the depths of night,
\par When dazzled with excess of light,
\par We bow before the heavenly voice
\par Which bids bewildered souls rejoice:
\par Though love wax cold, and faith grow dim,
\par This is My Son: O hear ye Him!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

